==Strategy==
The biggest difference between Floor 21 and [[Attack on R-Cyclone (Expert)|Attack on R-Cyclone]] is the addition of hard-hitting midrangers to the enemy formation: Capy and Christmas D. Using [[Fortune Teller Cat (Rare Cat)|Fortune Teller Cat]] or [[Pirate Cat (Rare Cat)|Pirate Cat]] becomes counterproductive, as their [[Knockback|knockback]] effects can push the Red Cyclone away, putting all other units within reach of enemy midrangers. Income is also rather scarce, so make the best out of them when the Shy Boys arrive. Traditional Meatshielding proves to be effective if Red Cyclone has been properly countered by CC units, as most other enemies (especially Capy) are weak against them.

To capitalize on [[:Category:Anti-Red Cats|anti-Red]] and [[:Category:Anti-Floating Cats|anti-Floating]] units, it is recommended you have 100% [[Blood Fruit|Blood]] and [[Sky Fruit]] [[Treasure]]s from all three chapters of [[Into the Future]] when attempting this stage.

===Recommended Units===
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] - A very strong specialist LD attacker, Courier's Massive Damage ability against Red enemies makes it an excellent addition to this stage. When given the chance, Courier can melt through these threats like a hot knife through butter.
*[[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|iCat]] - iCat's 100% chance to Freeze Red enemies for 2 seconds helps at the start of the battle and against Red Cyclone, but with its low range and long recharge it should not be your only source of defense.
*[[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo]] - Sanzo, being a midranged disposable CC, has 20% chance to Slow Floating enemies for 4 seconds, and can act as a second line of defense to delay Red Cyclone in case if iCat falls. Any potential drawbacks are easily negated by the fact Red Cyclone has only one knockback, and therefore won't reposition. This allows your LD units to continue whittling other Red threats with ease.

